# Error Handling Rules (full doc: docs/error-handling.md)

## Core Principle

Every layer uses `AppError` with category-based typing. No raw `Error`, no plain strings.
Use `Err.*` factories — they log automatically.

## Critical Rules

- Use `Err.*` factories, not `new Error()` or string throws
- Include `service`, `operation`, `context`, `cause` in every error
- NEVER log then throw `Err.*` — factories already log (avoids double-logging)
- Re-throw `AppError` unchanged; normalize unknowns with `toAppError()`
- Use `safeFetch` + `httpResponseToError` for HTTP requests
- Check `category`/`code` instead of parsing error messages

## Decision Helpers

- `isRetryable(error)` — Network, Timeout, Server, RateLimit
- `requiresLogin(error)` — Auth + UNAUTHORIZED or SESSION_EXPIRED
- `isNotFound(error)` — NOT_FOUND or RECORD_NOT_FOUND

For full layer-specific patterns, code examples, and migration checklist: read docs/error-handling.md
